 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It' an optical illusion. We see it with watercolors too. The wet layer in front of dry one makes the whole thing look darker. Sorry about that. You can help it by spending a bit more time between wet layers, so the surface is dry enough not to show the shadow. Yes, hold a bright light at it. If you can see the layers separately, then it's dry enough and you' fine. If not, let it dry longer. Then work on a dry layer between them. Or use a clear varnish that doesn't change the color much.",
